Package: fgrepl
Type: Package
Title: Fast Parallel String Matching via RE2 and RcppParallel
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Kyle", "Haynes", email = "kyle@kylehaynes.com.au", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides a drop-in replacement for grepl() that uses Google's RE2
    regex engine (linear-time, no catastrophic backtracking) parallelised across
    all CPU cores via Intel TBB through RcppParallel. Typically 10-50x faster
    than base grepl() on large character vectors. Note: RE2 does not support
    PCRE-only features such as backreferences or lookahead/lookbehind assertions.
License: Apache License (>= 2.0)
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
Imports:
    Rcpp (>= 1.0.0),
    RcppParallel (>= 5.0.0)
LinkingTo:
    Rcpp,
    RcppParallel
SystemRequirements: C++14, GNU make
